</form>

### Configuration

<form markdown="1" method="POST" action="/update.php" target="progressFrame">
<input type="hidden" name="csrf_token" value="<?=htmlspecialchars($csrfToken, ENT_QUOTES, 'UTF-8')?>">
<input type="hidden" name="#file" value="unraid-vsock-sensors/unraid-vsock-sensors.cfg">
<input type="hidden" name="#command" value="/plugins/unraid-vsock-sensors/service.sh">
<input type="hidden" name="#arg[1]" value="restart">

_(VSOCK port)_:
: <input type="number" name="PORT" value="<?=$port?>" min="1" max="4294967294" required>

<blockquote class="inline_help">
The Proxmox receiver and the Unraid publisher must use the same VSOCK port.
</blockquote>

_(Unraid SMART polling interval)_:
: <?=htmlspecialchars($pollDisplay, ENT_QUOTES)?>

<blockquote class="inline_help">
This read-only value comes from Unraid Disk Settings. While the poll_attributes heartbeat is healthy, Unraid's temp and spundown values are authoritative. If the heartbeat becomes stale, UVSS temporarily reads SMART directly with standby protection.
</blockquote>

<?php if (!$pollValid): ?>
<p class="red">
The Unraid <code>poll_attributes</code> value is missing or invalid. The daemon keeps the last valid heartbeat interval; before the first valid read after startup it uses 30 seconds. It does not modify Unraid settings.
</p>
<?php elseif ($pollAttributes === 0): ?>
<p class="red">
Automatic SMART polling is disabled in Unraid. UVSS does not start automatic fallback: active disks are unavailable, while standby disks retain their synthetic standby state.
</p>
<?php elseif ($pollAttributes > 60): ?>
<p class="red">
Unraid polls SMART data every <?=$pollAttributes?> seconds. Fan control may therefore react with several minutes of delay. Reduce the SMART polling interval in Unraid Disk Settings if faster reaction is required.
</p>
<?php endif; ?>

_(HBA monitoring)_:
: <select name="HBA_MODE">
<option value="enabled" <?=$hbaMode === 'enabled' ? 'selected' : ''?>>Enabled</option>
<option value="disabled" <?=$hbaMode === 'disabled' ? 'selected' : ''?>>Disabled</option>
</select>

<blockquote class="inline_help">
Enabled collects HBA temperatures using the backend selected below. Disabled explicitly clears the HBA inventory when the host agent restarts.
</blockquote>

_(HBA backend)_:
: <select id="hba-backend" name="HBA_BACKEND">
<option value="mpt3ctl" <?=$hbaBackend === 'mpt3ctl' ? 'selected' : ''?>>Native /dev/mpt3ctl</option>
<option value="storcli" <?=$hbaBackend === 'storcli' ? 'selected' : ''?>>StorCLI</option>
</select>

<blockquote class="inline_help">
The native backend requires a controller handled by <code>mpt3sas</code> and access to <code>/dev/mpt3ctl</code>. It does not require an external utility but is experimental and has not yet been validated across a broad range of controllers and firmware versions.<br><br>
The StorCLI backend requires StorCLI to be installed, for example through the <a href="https://forums.unraid.net/topic/192112-plugin-storcli64/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">storcli64 Unraid plugin</a>.
</blockquote>

_(HBA refresh interval)_:
: <select id="hba-interval" name="HBA_INTERVAL" data-current="<?=htmlspecialchars($hbaInterval, ENT_QUOTES)?>">
</select>
<p id="hba-interval-warning" class="red" hidden></p>

<blockquote class="inline_help">
Default uses 15 seconds with native <code>mpt3ctl</code> and 30 seconds with StorCLI. StorCLI uses a longer default because its command-based collection is more expensive than the native MPT3 ioctl path. Each new HBA state is pushed to Proxmox.
</blockquote>

&nbsp;

: <input type="submit" value="_(Apply)_">
</form>

### Disk policies

<p>
Auto excludes disks physically connected through USB. Include and Exclude override this choice. If the physical bus cannot be determined, Auto includes the disk for thermal safety. The Unraid boot flash device is always excluded.
</p>

<?php if ($diskListState === 'daemon' || $diskListState === 'transport'): ?>

<p class="red">
Disk inventory unavailable. <?php if ($diskListState === 'daemon'): ?>The unraid-vsock-sensors daemon is not running.<?php else: ?>The daemon could not be reached (<?php echo htmlspecialchars($diskListError, ENT_QUOTES, 'UTF-8'); ?>).<?php endif; ?> Start the service or check the daemon log; disk policies cannot be listed until the daemon is reachable.
</p>

<?php elseif ($diskListState === 'error'): ?>

<p class="red">
Disk inventory unavailable. The daemon returned an inventory or control API error (<?php echo htmlspecialchars($diskListError, ENT_QUOTES, 'UTF-8'); ?>). Check the daemon log; this is not a policy validation failure, so disk policies cannot be reset from here.
</p>

<?php elseif ($diskPoliciesInvalid): ?>

<p class="red">
Disk policies are invalid. The daemon keeps the last valid policies already loaded; after a cold start with no valid policy state yet, it uses Auto. Reset the file to return to a clean Auto configuration.
</p>

<form id="uvss-reset-disk-policies" class="uvss-control-form" method="POST" action="/plugins/unraid-vsock-sensors/uvss_action.php">
<input type="hidden" name="csrf_token" value="<?=htmlspecialchars($csrfToken, ENT_QUOTES, 'UTF-8')?>">
<input type="hidden" name="action" value="reset-disk-policies">
<button type="submit">Reset disk policies</button>
</form>

<?php elseif (count($diskRows) === 0): ?>

<p>No disks are currently known.</p>

<?php else: ?>

<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Name</th>
<th>Unraid ID</th>
<th>Device</th>
<th>emhttpd transport</th>
<th>Physical bus</th>
<th>Policy</th>
<th>Selection</th>
<th>Eligibility</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>

<?php foreach ($diskRows as $diskRow):
    $diskID = (string)($diskRow['id'] ?? '');
    $diskName = (string)($diskRow['name'] ?? '');
    $diskPolicy = (string)($diskRow['policy'] ?? 'auto');
    $diskSelected = ($diskRow['selected'] ?? false) === true;
    $diskEligible = ($diskRow['eligible'] ?? false) === true;
    $diskValidationError = (string)($diskRow['validation_error'] ?? '');
    $isFlash = strcasecmp($diskName, 'flash') === 0;
?>

<tr>
<td><?=htmlspecialchars($diskName, ENT_QUOTES, 'UTF-8')?></td>
<td><?=htmlspecialchars($diskID, ENT_QUOTES, 'UTF-8')?></td>
<td><?=htmlspecialchars(
    ($diskRow['device'] ?? '') === ''
        ? '—'
        : '/dev/' . $diskRow['device'],
    ENT_QUOTES,
    'UTF-8'
)?></td>
<td><?=htmlspecialchars(
    ($diskRow['transport'] ?? '') === ''
        ? '—'
        : $diskRow['transport'],
    ENT_QUOTES,
    'UTF-8'
)?></td>
<td><?=htmlspecialchars(
    (string)($diskRow['bus'] ?? 'unknown'),
    ENT_QUOTES,
    'UTF-8'
)?></td>
<td>

<?php if ($diskID !== '' && !$isFlash): ?>

<form class="uvss-disk-policy-form uvss-control-form" method="POST" action="/plugins/unraid-vsock-sensors/uvss_action.php">
<input type="hidden" name="csrf_token" value="<?=htmlspecialchars($csrfToken, ENT_QUOTES, 'UTF-8')?>">
<input type="hidden" name="action" value="set-disk-policy">
<input type="hidden" name="disk_id" value="<?=htmlspecialchars($diskID, ENT_QUOTES, 'UTF-8')?>">
<select name="policy">
<option value="auto" <?=$diskPolicy === 'auto' ? 'selected' : ''?>>Auto</option>
<option value="include" <?=$diskPolicy === 'include' ? 'selected' : ''?>>Include</option>
<option value="exclude" <?=$diskPolicy === 'exclude' ? 'selected' : ''?>>Exclude</option>
</select>
<button type="submit">_(Apply)_</button>
</form>

<?php else: ?>

<?=htmlspecialchars(ucfirst($diskPolicy), ENT_QUOTES, 'UTF-8')?>

<?php endif; ?>

</td>
<td><?=$diskSelected ? 'Included' : 'Excluded'?></td>
<td>
<?php if ($diskEligible): ?>
Eligible
<?php else: ?>
<span class="red">Not eligible</span><?php if ($diskValidationError !== ''): ?> - <?=htmlspecialchars($diskValidationError, ENT_QUOTES, 'UTF-8')?><?php endif; ?>
